 {
  "id": 20,
  "course_id": 1,
  "name": "AC Quiz #2: 2nd Derivatives, Function Behavior, Differentiability & MVT",
  "description": "<p>The only homework due for Day 2 this week (10/19-10/23) is to prepare for a quiz in class on the material covered to date. Use the work we have completed in class and the homework assignments (along with the associated KEYs) to prepare, focusing more on concepts or problem-types for which you feel you need the most review. You may come to see me in conference with any additional questions you may have.</p>\n<p><strong>Topics To Be Covered On Quiz:</strong></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>1.</strong>&nbsp; Interpreting 2<sup>nd</sup> Derivatives In Context</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>2.</strong>&nbsp; Relationships Between f(x), f'(x), f''(x) and Function Behavior (Slope, Roots, Inflection Points, Concavity, Increasing, Decreasing, Etc...)</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>3.</strong>&nbsp; Differentiability: Formal Definition; Graphical Characteristics; Algebraic Determination</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>4.</strong>&nbsp; The Mean Value Theorem: Formal Definition, Algebraic Determination &amp; Application</p>",
